          "update_time": 1792983785.055,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "The first correction gives a half-power gain, provided we also retain one more Riemann–Siegel term. The bounds are \\(O(|G|X^{-5/4})\\) for the field, spatial derivatives through order three, and first time derivative, with residual \\(O(|G|X^{-7/4})\\). The formula still retains a bounded correction integral; it does not achieve outer-scale accuracy at fixed negative time."
            ]
          },
          "status": "finished_successfully",
          "end_turn": false,
