          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Derived and saved in [Note10](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-5/01_heat_density_asymptotics/ansatz/notes/10_FIRST_NEGATIVE_TIME_EVOLUTION_CORRECTION_20261025.md). For each exact gamma mode \\(h\\), with \\(\\beta=\\partial_z\\log h\\), the correction is\n\\[\nh e^{T\\beta^2}\\left[1+\\beta'(T+2T^2\\beta^2)\\right].\n\\]\n\nRetaining the next RS term and a bounded correction integral proves, uniformly on \\(1\\le T\\le2\\) and the full buffered charts:\n\n- Field, spatial derivatives through three, and first time error: \\(O(|G|X^{-5/4})\\), improving by \\(X^{-1/2}\\).\n- Actual residual and its first spatial derivative: \\(O(|G|X^{-7/4})\\).\n\nThe remaining outer-relative allowance is\n\\[\nX^{-5/4}e^{T L^2/16},\\qquad L=\\log(X/(4\\pi)),\n\\]\nwhich still grows at fixed \\(T\\). This limits the bound; it is not an error lower bound.\n\nProgress, assessment, handoff return, and chat history are recorded. AN03 is closed at this bounded scope; A02 remains Partial. The formula retains all arithmetic modes and the RS integral. Assessment is internal, same-model only.\n\nNext: **Analysis — Sol**, manuscript integration under the prepared AN04 packet."
